{"term":"enormity","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:62ca45d8087ba6cae0","definition":"Deviation from what is normal or standard; irregularity, abnormality.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["anomalousness"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["enormous","enormously","enormousness","norm","normative","normatively","normativity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enormity#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a756bf49654b4d1475","definition":"Deviation from moral normality; extreme wickedness, nefariousness, or cruelty.","example":"Not until the war ended and journalists were able to enter Cambodia did the world really become aware of the enormity of Pol Pot’s oppression.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["atrociousness"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["enormous","enormously","enormousness","norm","normative","normatively","normativity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enormity#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:57dd58471f83663a8b","definition":"A breach of law or morality; a transgression, an act of evil or wickedness.","example":"Yet she appeared confident in innocence, and did not tremble, although gazed on and execrated by thousands; for all the kindness which her beauty might otherwise have excited, was obliterated in the minds of the spectators by the imagination of the enormity she was supposed to have committed.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["desecration","violation"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["enormous","enormously","enormousness","norm","normative","normatively","normativity"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors",